  "verbalization": "Streptenol C is implicated in the interaction with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which serves as a common target across multiple pathways. This complex is engaged by different compounds, including Rha(a1-3)[coumaroyl(3-OH)(-4)]Glc(b)-O-EtPh, Docosanoic acid, pentyl ester, and Sid24841469, all of which ultimately target SN12K1. The shared involvement of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex suggests a potential mechanism where Streptenol C may modulate the activity of this complex, possibly through direct or indirect interactions. The evidence supports a role for Streptenol C in influencing the function of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which in turn affects SN12K1. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of the complex in mediating the effects of Streptenol C on SN12K1, with the exact nature of the interaction remaining to be elucidated.",
